{"type":"assistant","uuid":"7ef724d6-28ba-42cf-96b8-d0bbe6a0ea49","session_id":"626f5182-b9a4-4090-abf6-af597cd80f07","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"7ef724d6-28ba-42cf-96b8-d0bbe6a0ea49","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me summarize my diagnosis and implement the fix.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n**Root Cause: Race condition in `QueueFragment.onFragmentLoaded()`**\n\nWhen the last item is swiped away:\n1. `onSwiped()` calls `DBWriter.removeQueueItem()` and shows the Snackbar\n2. `onEventMainThread(QueueEvent)` receives the REMOVED event → calls `notifyItemRemoved()` and then `onFragmentLoaded()`\n3. `onFragmentLoaded()` immediately toggles `recyclerView.setVisibility(View.GONE)` and `txtvEmpty.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE)`\n4. **The visibility toggle happens WHILE item removal animations are still running** — before the RecyclerView finishes laying out\n5. When the user taps \"Undo\" and `addQueueItemAt()` fires an ADDED event → `notifyItemInserted(position)` is called\n6. The RecyclerView is in an inconsistent state (visibility was toggled mid-animation), so the re-inserted item ends up off-screen\n\n**Fix**: Defer the visibility toggle using `recyclerView.post()` so it executes after all pending adapter notifications and animations settle.\n\nNow let me apply the fix:\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
