{"type":"assistant","uuid":"5bb9a892-8aec-4db5-9768-807a98bb60bb","session_id":"626f5182-b9a4-4090-abf6-af597cd80f07","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"5bb9a892-8aec-4db5-9768-807a98bb60bb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\n### Bug: \"Undo with last list item does not work\"\n\n**Root Cause:** Race condition in `QueueFragment.onFragmentLoaded()` where the RecyclerView visibility is toggled (`View.GONE`/`View.VISIBLE`) *before* pending item removal animations complete.\n\n**What happens when the last item is swiped:**\n1. `onSwiped()` calls `DBWriter.removeQueueItem()` (async DB write) and shows the Snackbar\n2. The REMOVED event fires → `notifyItemRemoved(0)` starts the item removal animation\n3. `onFragmentLoaded()` immediately hides the RecyclerView and shows the empty TextView\n4. **The visibility toggle happens while the RecyclerView is mid-animation**, putting it in an inconsistent state\n5. When \"Undo\" taps → `addQueueItemAt()` fires ADDED event → `notifyItemInserted()` is called on a RecyclerView that was toggled mid-animation\n6. The restored item renders off-screen\n\n**Fix:** Defer the visibility toggle using `recyclerView.post()` so it executes on the next frame, after all pending adapter notifications and animations settle.\n\n### Patch file created:\n**`patch-fix-bug-1130.patch`**\n\nThe fix changes only one file: `app/src/main/java/de/danoeh/antennapod/fragment/QueueFragment.java`\n\n- **Lines changed:** In `onFragmentLoaded()`, wrapped the `if(queue == null || queue.size() == 0)` visibility toggle in `recyclerView.post(() -> { ... })`\n- **Impact:** Minimal — only defers an existing visibility check; no new logic or behavior changes\n- **Build:** Confirmed `BUILD SUCCESSFUL` with no errors or warnings"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76573,"output_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":76032,"total_tokens":76953}}}
